{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '99,130p;194,270p' AGENTS.md; rg -n '\"'^## D(24|28|186|198|260|263|274|354|359|368|694|711|719|721|722|726)'\"\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"   the work before its first step and after its terminal outcome. Each cell names the transition, what is written, and the date every\n   read and write uses.\n2. **Value × reader.** Every value a change writes, against every reader of it (found by searching the field) and every input source the\n   value can come from. A rule over a kind of data lists every writer of that kind. A change to how often something fires is counted\n   against every reader of its output.\n3. **New path × old checks.** For a new input, derived value, mode or changed data shape: every check the old path passes, and whether\n   the new one meets it. A changed shape re-derives every check written for the old one.\n4. **Prior decisions.** The decisions searched for the mechanism by name; any decision that rejected or bounded it is quoted in the\n   design and in the question to Alex.\n\n- A contract over text or shapes states the closed set of what passes (a full match); anything else fails or is not judged. Enumerate\n  the accepted set against every context and reader it meets before the first edit.\n- **Code owns identity, never importance.** Before building a closed list, enum or gate, write which decision it takes from the model\n  and whether that decision is identity (\"are these the same thing?\") or judgement (\"does this matter?\"); build only the identity part.\n  A list of what matters is at most a hint shown to the model (Alex, 2026-10-25: \"你这个做法难道不是非常的限死吗？永远都是一堆财务指标，真正的观点呢？\").\n- **No case-fitted fix.** A hand list, a special path or a rule fitted to the case in view fixes that case and breaks the next. First ask\n  whether the judge had the material and the definition it needed, and whether a typed field is missing; run the proposal against the\n  existing tests and the gold for a counter-example before building (D167: \"我不要 hardcode 解法 it's premature optimization, not general root fix\").\n- A blind review measures the tables. A serious finding they do not hold shows a missing dimension: add it and walk every row again,\n  never answer the finding alone. Code starts when the review finds nothing serious. A design whose core contract is still open is a\n  question, not something to build.\n- A foundation's acceptance carries a size and speed budget from its first control, not only correctness.\n\n## 3. Writing code\n\n- **One owner.** A rule lives where the data is written, and refuses: a warning that lets the run continue is a silent failure. Fix the\n  writer and delete its duplicate implementations in the same change; when a fix lands in one consumer, search every consumer of the\n  same key or rule.\n- **Code over prose.** A contract that code or a schema can enforce (an enum over allowed keys, a shape) is enforced there, and stays out\n  of prompts and documents.\n- **One word per concept.** The glossary in `docs/prd/00-system.md` (section Glossary; D36, D163) names each concept once, and\n  `docs/check.py` fails on a word it rules out. A new concept gets its row and its ruled-out words in the same change; a new ruled-out\n## 6. Writing prompts\n\n- **The prompt carries the standard, not new rules.** Every sentence about what to keep, reject, weigh or open traces to a line of the\n  step's standard (§7.1) or a decision; a sentence with no such line is a proposal for Alex, not an edit. A reject sentence must not\n  remove what the standard keeps: a missing amount, date or scale is never on its own a reason to drop a statement an analyst would note;\n  its weight is judged apart and may be lower (D240, Alex: \"我不是和你说过不要这么死板吗？这个证据显然是有意义的，不一定什么条件数据时间都要满足，你应该把它记录下来，只是可能档位低一点\").\n- **The prompt audit runs after every measurement and before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`). The whole\n  request (system, every category block, the fixed user sentences, every schema description and example) is read against the standard\n  clause by clause, in both directions, with a blind read-only second reader: each clause is consistent, contradicts, keeps wider, keeps\n  narrower or has no source. The procedure is audited too: a rule that decides by another test than the standard's, or an exception\n  written wider than the standard scopes it, contradicts the standard even when every sentence quotes it. Each failure class of the last\n  measurement gets one row (the request sentence, the standard's line, a verdict: contradiction, missing, abstract, misread, not the\n  prompt) in the arm's design document before a fix is written; a fix that answers a bench miss rather than a sentence is not written.\n  Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你需要同时仔细检查prompt和判法准则矛盾的问题，出现很多次了，你应该要做很细的检查\"; 2026-11-02: \"这个就是prompt的问题，你有没有深度的看promt 然后映射问题找矛盾\n  … 你应该看着prompt，然后对比失败的trace，然后仔细的根据尺子做对比，并且我们prompt的principle 也要带入，是尝试教他general hedge fund\n  analyst skill, 不是要hardcode或是benchmark farming；你把这个写成一个skill 以后固定跑，不然你每次都没有检讨到\".\n- **A test the model must apply to each statement is a check at the very end of the same prompt.** In one pass the model keeps what\n  looks like evidence and cites a rule afterwards; asked afterwards it judges correctly. So a closing check reads the list back and\n  returns only what passes, in the same call: the standard's own test, then its not-kept rows, each with its own boundary and the\n  standard's own examples, audited like any prompt text; a lost entry is judged by a blind reader. Alex, 2026-10-30: \"这个完全就是再prompt 的最后面要求做完一遍基于'你刚才说的复核条件'再跑一次；写在同一个提示词里面\".\n- **A prompt serves every company, never the bench.** Every analyst prompt is a general hedge-fund brain: each rule and example reads the\n  same for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip maker. Examples teach from varied domains; none names the covered company, its\n  products or its numbers, and none is taken from a test article. A fix is written from the standard and from the request read as the\n  model reads it, not from the bench's misses, and a prompt is scrubbed for one-company or one-industry wording before any measurement.\n  Alex, 2026-10-29 (D237): \"It needs to be general purpose as a hedge fund brain. I keep on telling you this, and you keep on cherry\n  picking the results just to meet the metrics or the benchmarks\".\n- **Never grow a prompt to fix quality.** Read the whole request (system, schema, payload) as the model reads it, and list every\n  contradiction, rule written for another case, instruction that forces the defect, reference the model cannot read, payload field the\n  answer does not need, and call doing several jobs. Cut, merge or split. Add an instruction only when the audit shows one is missing,\n  and remove at least as much elsewhere. Report characters and prompt tokens before and after; growth needs a written reason.\n- **Trace a miss to the raw answer first.** Class it as not written, refused (by which check) or split. Check that the request shows what\n  the answer needs and the schema can express it before changing any wording.\n- **An example is an instruction.** It must agree with the standard, the schema and the code that reads the answer, or it goes.\n- **A classification the model must make is written as a closed set with examples:** two or three examples per class, the procedure\n  (walk the whole page, first paragraph to last) and the stopping point (\"a page with eight such statements yields eight evidence\n  items\"). An abstract clause (\"a material statement\") is a coin flip per send. The examples are not growth to avoid; the abstract clause\n  they replace is cut.\n- **Check before the send, at no cost.** Write one answer that follows the prompt and run every code check on it: a request never asks\n  for what a check refuses, and a retry that repairs a refusal is a symptom, not handling. Read every contract line against each gold\n  case it must accept and reject. Rebuild a stored request from the stored request, never from a ledger that moves, and check every\n  identity before a paid send.\n- **Build where code decides.** A decision code can make is moved out of the model, not sampled (identity only, §2).\n\n## 7. Measuring and iterating\n\n### 7.1 The ruler\n\n- **One ruler.** Every gold, judge, prompt and acceptance uses the one standard named before the first arm. A second ruler in use (an old\n  reference, a judge's rubric, a prompt's own categories) is a defect, fixed before anything is measured (D241, Alex: \"我们今天一直浪费时间在不同标准之间来回\").\n- **The frozen ruler (D261, D262; 2026-11-02)** remains the standard for existing measurements and historical comparisons until a separately reviewed replacement is established. For future evidence scoring (D372), combine the existing gold's core and supporting as helpful, treat its not-kept entries as unhelpful, and leave optional entries neutral; this does not alter the frozen files. Its pieces, with the hashes code checks:\n  1. The extraction standard: `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`, its version 5 (version 3 as signed in D243, with D248's seven\n     boundaries and D250's four evidence boundaries and counting unit); the gold `docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v5/` (dev sha256 `6f9476bb…`, test `af2145cd…`, recorded\n     in `golden-v5.sha256`). There is no version 6.\n  2. The questions: golden-v5's must_open / may_open (questions standard version 3) and the seeds `poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json`\n     (`fca16f42…`, 22 questions). The seeds are part of the ruler: the judgement scorer refuses a run whose seed questions differ; a new\n     seed set is a new ruler version, opened only by Alex's decision.\n  3. The judgement ruler (D3): `docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/`: `ruler-v1.md` (the definition), `reader-brief.md`,\n     `packet-v1.json` (golden-v5's 309 items, `53d1e8b4…`), `questions-v1.json` (the 22 seeds plus the Ohio guarantee, `30854180…`),\n     `gold-v1.json` = reader B's answers (`636c056d…`, in `gold-v1.sha256`), `score_judgement.py` (refuses any other sha256 or ruler\n     version), `corrections-v1.json` (dated records only, printed with every score, never merged).\n\n  None of these files changes again (`tests/test_frozen_rulers.py` fails the suite when a hash moves; Alex, 2026-11-02: \"你的尺子做出来和金标真的不能再动了，\n  已经造成了3天的各种漂移，非常的严重 … 我们做完的review过的尺子金标不能再动了\"). A defect found later is a dated correction record beside the gold,\n  with its reason and its before and after, printed with every score and never merged in. Every measurement names the gold version it used. A new piece (the D2\n  matter-to-question mapping, not yet built, is one) is an addition recorded as such, never an edit of these. A new version of any piece\n  exists only by Alex's decision, derives its gold from scratch, and old scores are never compared with it. A disagreement between the\n  system and the gold is a gap in the system to close (D263), never a case for the ruler. A suspected inconsistency between gold and\n  standard no longer stops an arm: record the concern separately, continue scoring on the unchanged frozen gold, and disclose it with the results (D373).\n  What it measures: extraction against the gold's items, questions against must_open / may_open, the judgement at the window end\n  2026-07-14 against reader B's ranges (a numeric question agrees when the gold range overlaps the chosen rung's band, a yes/no question\n  when the answers match). What it does not measure: the judgement's daily path, and whether evidence was filed under the right question.\n- **The extraction standard** (piece 1) is the extraction step's PRD, signed by Alex on 2026-10-29 (D243: \"其他几条的意见我都ok，sign off\"),\n  which replaced the first version (D229: \"按照这套标准来开始做测量，这条标准不要漂移\"). It holds the ledger's three records, the five question\n  types, the opening tests, the evidence rule and its reject list, source tiers, weight, and how a prompt change is written, measured and\n  iterated. No arm, gold, judge or prompt adds a rule, an example or a weight the page does not hold; a change is a recorded decision in\n  Alex's words first, then a new version of the page, then a drift review.\n- **A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again** (D261). Reviewed means readers who did not write it have read it\n433:## D24 · 2026-10-16 · Financial reports are not streamed; pull mode reads them when a thesis needs them\n567:## D28 · 2026-10-18 · Financial reports stream again\n2476:## D186 · 2026-10-26 · Asset-thesis rungs describe business outcomes; the favourable end is registered per thesis\n2559:## D198 · 2026-10-27 · A judgement reads the evidence in view, not everything in force\n3049:## D260 · 2026-11-02 · A judgement is a forecast against a reference: the rung the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects; the answer states the reference and the implied outcome (judging-v6)\n3069:## D263 · 2026-11-02 · The judge is written to the frozen gold's own reasoning (judging-v7, poc-v91); a gap to the gold is closed in the judge, not re-measured\n3151:## D274 · 2026-11-03 · The extraction production prompt is frozen at v74i (`poc-v108`); the unadopted variants are retired\n3685:## D354 · 2026-11-03 · Steps 3 and 4 (opening and matching questions, judging them) are frozen as `poc-v108` runs them, after three draws on the frozen extraction\n3798:## D359 · 2026-11-04 · The code builds only the frozen prompts (extraction v74i, judging-v7); old worktrees removed; the preflight reads the one-decider requests\n3960:## D368 · 2026-11-05 · Alex's answers to the seven items left open by the consolidation\n10439:## D694 · 2026-11-21 · Alex chooses A: links leave filing alone; new matching and judging versions open for linking; the July test after the council passes the $0 proof\n10660:## D711 · 2026-11-21 · Pilot pair 1 is inconclusive (control double refusal); the comparison is closed; council round 37 recommends a citation-only judge version to Alex\n10825:## D719 · 2026-11-22 · Alex stops the citation line: judging-v12 is not adopted; poc-v118 stays the product\n10859:## D721 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 43/43b: the double-count premise is partly falsified by the frozen gold; recommend closing the design with nothing to build; D711's H4 reading corrected\n10892:## D722 · 2026-11-22 · Alex closes the double-count design with nothing changed\n10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'wc -l docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{DESIGN,RESULT}.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"     127 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/DESIGN.md\n      93 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md\n     220 total\n     1\t# judging-v13: related number questions judged together, with a checked calculation (design v1, for council round 46)\n     2\t\n     3\tOpened by Alex (D726) for the bounded test of D725. Harness-only until a later decision: no product configuration names it, and\n     4\tthe ordinary launchers refuse it (D359, D723). The frozen judge (judging-v7, poc-v118) is unchanged.\n     5\t\n     6\t## 1. What changes\n     7\t\n     8\t| Piece | judging-v7 (today) | judging-v13 |\n     9\t|---|---|---|\n    10\t| Unit | one question per call | one **family** per call: the number questions of one company and fiscal period whose quantities overlap (a total and its segment or product line, a level and its growth). Each keeps its own answer |\n    11\t| Who forms a family | none (0 dependencies) | **declared** for the test from the stored cases. Production would need a matching version that names the relation (`part_of`, `same_base`). Undirected; the relation names which is the part or the base |\n    12\t| Evidence shown | each question's own evidence in view (D198) | the union of the members' evidence in view, each passage once with its attribution; themes once |\n    13\t| Previous conclusion | rung and reasons, cut at 800 characters, unmarked | each member's previous rung and outcome, labelled \"our earlier forecast, not a source\"; its figures cannot fill a source or reference slot (check C5) |\n    14\t| Answer | prose fields plus one answer-wide citation list | a **calculation** (labelled figures) plus one answer per member that points to its outcome figure (§2) |\n    15\t| Code checks | rung range, ids, pushes, non-empty fields | the same, plus C1–C6 (§3) |\n    16\t| Failure | refused twice: the question is left as it was | refused twice: the family's forecasts are recorded as **unresolved**; no member gets an incompatible update |\n    17\t\n    18\tThe system prompt is judging-v7's text, unchanged in its standard (the frozen gold's reasoning: reference, run-rate, discounting,\n    19\tsizing, identities, consistency). Added: one block on how to write the calculation (§2), and the family header. Growth is reported\n    20\twith the build.\n    21\t\n    22\t## 2. The answer format (closed set; the schema enforces shape, code enforces C1–C6)\n    23\t\n    24\t```\n    25\tfigures: [ { id: \"f1\",\n    26\t             what: { population, measure, scope, period },   # e.g. NVIDIA / revenue / Data Center segment / FY2027 Q3\n    27\t             kind: \"source\" | \"computed\" | \"estimate\",\n    28\t             value | low+high, unit: \"USD bn\" | \"%\" | \"units\" | ...,\n    29\t             source: \"<evidence id>\"           # kind source only: a shown passage\n    30\t             inputs: [\"f2\",\"f3\"], operation: \"sum\" | \"difference\" | \"product\" | \"ratio\" | \"growth\" | \"share\"   # kind computed only\n    31\t             basis: \"<why>\", rests_on: [\"f…\", \"<evidence id>\", …]   # kind estimate only: the judge's judgement, stated as such\n    32\t           } ]\n    33\treference: { figure: \"f…\" } | { none_supplied: true, why }\n    34\tanswers:   [ { view_id, outcome: \"f…\", rung, reasons, cites, cites_views: [], pushes, theme_pushes, changed, why_changed } ]\n    35\t```\n    36\t\n    37\t- **source:** a figure stated in a shown passage, as stated: a value or a range in a unit.\n    38\t- **computed:** a figure derived from other figures by one named operation.\n    39\t- **estimate:** any figure the judge chooses. This covers a discount, a reasoned range, an overlap assumption, a growth carried forward\n    40\t  and a scenario. It is allowed, and it is labelled as the judge's.\n    41\t\n    42\t  The frozen gold uses estimates throughout:\n    43\t  - **q01:** a second-half range of $228–262B resting on growth acceleration, compute tracking, the Rubin ramp and the Vera target,\n    44\t    with no fixed increment;\n    45\t  - **q02:** a 92–93% share of q01's total;\n    46\t  - **q19:** the $20B target discounted for two selling quarters and four million units;\n    47\t  - **q22:** FY2028 from q01's base, widened.\n    48\t- One `what` key (population, measure, scope, period) per role and scenario: two figures with the same key must agree (C4). A\n    49\t  guide and a forecast of the same quarter differ in `what.measure` (\"guidance\" against \"forecast\"), not silently.\n    50\t\n    51\t## 3. What code checks (identity and arithmetic only; AGENTS §2)\n    52\t\n    53\t| Check | Rule | Refuses |\n    54\t|---|---|---|\n    55\t| C1 | a `source` figure's value (or both range ends) and unit appear in the cited passage's shown text (normalised: $, billion/bn/B, %, ±; 0.5% tolerance) | an amount absent from its quote; a source that was not shown |\n    56\t| C2 | a `computed` figure recomputes from its inputs by its operation (0.5% or 0.1 unit tolerance) | a wrong sum or share |\n    57\t| C3 | for every declared `part_of` relation, the part's figure is at most the whole's, for the same period and scenario | a segment quarter above the company's quarter |\n    58\t| C4 | figures with the same `what` key agree (equal, or ranges that coincide) | two values for one shared quantity |\n    59\t| C5 | `reference.figure` is a `source` figure from a shown passage whose speaker is not the system, or `none_supplied`; a previous conclusion is never a source | the system's own forecast presented as the market's |\n    60\t| C6 | each answer's rung is the rung whose band contains its `outcome` figure (a range: the rung containing its midpoint, and the range named in the reasons) | a rung that does not match its own figure |\n    61\t\n    62\t**Recorded, not refused** (visible to readers and to the page):\n    63\t- **band-deciding estimates:** code recomputes the outcome with each `estimate` term removed or set to its neutral value. Where the rung\n    64\t  changes, it lists the estimate as deciding the band. This is arithmetic. Whether the estimate is supported is a reader's judgement in\n    65\t  the test.\n    66\t- **additions of two sources with no stated relation:** a `sum` of two `source` figures whose overlap the passages do not settle is\n    67\t  listed as an overlap estimate. The judge is told to write such a sum as an `estimate` with its basis.\n    68\t\n    69\t**The model keeps:** which drivers matter, how much, discounts, scenarios, and whether to step off the reference. Code never prefers\n    70\tguidance, prescribes a haircut, or refuses an estimate for being one.\n    71\t\n    72\t## 4. Tables (AGENTS §2)\n    73\t\n    74\t**Value × reader.**\n    75\t- **The calculation** (stored with the judgement): read by the checks, the readers' packets, later the page.\n    76\t- **`unresolved`:** read by the round (no update to members) and the bundle (\"Forecast unavailable\", D726).\n    77\t- **The family declaration:** read by the request builder and C3.\n    78\t- **Nothing in poc-v118 reads any of it.**\n    79\t\n    80\t**New path × old checks.**\n    81\t- v7's id, rung, push and theme checks apply per member answer.\n    82\t- `cites` must still name shown evidence. `cites_views` is empty: a family has no dependency reads.\n    83\t- v7's request bytes are unchanged; the frozen pins prove it.\n    84\t\n    85\t**State × event, for the test only:**\n    86\t- fixed stored snapshots;\n    87\t- one call per family per sample;\n    88\t- a refusal is retried once with the errors;\n    89\t- a second refusal makes the family unresolved, recorded;\n    90\t- no store is written beyond the harness archive.\n    91\t\n    92\tProduction state handling (a member closing, a new member opening mid-window, families changing) is out of the test and\n    93\tdesigned only if the test passes.\n    94\t\n    95\t**Prior decisions:**\n    96\t- D24, D28: bounded to the figures the open questions consume.\n    97\t- D198: the evidence in view, unioned.\n    98\t- D260, D263: the standard is unchanged.\n    99\t- D359, D723: no product launcher runs it.\n   100\t- D695: number questions only.\n   101\t- D711, D721: linking passed conclusions without assumptions.\n   102\t- D725, D726.\n   103\t\n   104\t## 5. The $0 gate (registered with D725; this design must pass it before any build of a sender)\n   105\t\n   106\t- **The reconstructions.** Hand-write, in the §2 format and faithful to the stored answers' own logic:\n   107\t  - **R1:** old-2 8729 (v14) and 8737 (v9) as one family on 09-20;\n   108\t  - **R2:** old-2 8734 (equity commitments: $25B + $18B + MediaTek + talks);\n   109\t  - **R3:** old-2 8595 (capex: 730/800 × $1.3T);\n   110\t  - **R4:** old-3 9166 (FY2028 Vera: guided above $40B, trimmed to $38–39B).\n   111\t- **The controls.** The four gold entries, q01, q02, q19 and q22, written in the format from `gold-v1.json`'s reasoning.\n   112\t- **The plants**, on copies of the controls:\n   113\t  - P1, a source amount absent from its quote;\n   114\t  - P2, a wrong sum;\n   115\t  - P3, an earlier system forecast as the reference.\n   116\t- **The checker:** `calc_check.py`, harness-only, run on all of them with the passages from the stored requests (and the gold\n   117\t  packet's items for the controls).\n   118\t- **Pass:**\n   119\t  - R1 fails C3 or C4;\n   120\t  - R2 lists the $18B sum as a band-deciding overlap estimate;\n   121\t  - R3 lists the scope bridge (a four-company 2026 spending figure against five-company capex) as a band-deciding estimate, or\n   122\t    fails C4;\n   123\t  - R4 lists the trim as a band-deciding estimate;\n   124\t  - every control passes, with its estimates visible;\n   125\t  - P1–P3 each fail their check.\n   126\t- **Stop:** any miss, or a valid control the format cannot express.\n   127\t- **Then:** Council B; the paid gate's ceiling goes to Alex.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RESULT.md; rg -n '\"'^## D72[4-9]|''^## D73[0-9]'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; ls docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Why the number answers cannot be trusted: council round 45/45b (2026-11-22, consensus, $0)\n     2\t\n     3\tAlex asked to step back and find which part of the design produces the unreliable numbers. The record:\n     4\t- `round45-brief.md`;\n     5\t- `claude-r45.md` (written before Codex);\n     6\t- `codex-r45.md` (an independent investigation, fresh thread `01a20501…`, read-only, no model calls);\n     7\t- `round45b-brief.md` and `codex-r45b.md` (the challenge round).\n     8\t\n     9\t## The answer\n    10\t\n    11\tThe system has no single, checked calculation behind its related numbers:\n    12\t- **Each number question is judged alone.** It rebuilds the company's numbers from its own slice of evidence, with its own bases and\n    13\t  its own reference.\n    14\t- **It publishes the result as prose.** Code cannot tell a sourced figure from an assumption, and never recomputes anything.\n    15\t\n    16\tContradictions between related questions and unsupported figures are what this design produces. They are not one prompt sentence's\n    17\tfault.\n    18\t\n    19\t## What the traces show (three finished poc-v118 draws, 07-01..09-20)\n    20\t\n    21\t- **Cross-question contradictions:**\n    22\t  - old-2 at 09-20: Data Center Q4 is about $146B, the whole company's Q4 about $127B. In old-1 on 09-20 it is $126B against $112.2B.\n    23\t  - A stated segment Q4 above the company Q4 on at least 13 of 26 paired post-earnings days in old-1, and at least 1 in old-2.\n    24\t  - Data Center's full year above total revenue's full year on 20 consecutive days in old-2 (08-26..09-14). Claude checked 08-28, 09-05\n    25\t    and 09-12: $419B, $422B and $414B against $407B.\n    26\t- **Different bases for the same quarter:** on 17 of 18 paired days, 09-15..09-20, Data Center used the $108B Q3 guide while total\n    27\t  revenue used a beat-adjusted Q3 of about $113.5B.\n    28\t- **Disjoint inputs:** old-2's two questions share 106 of about 1,300 linked evidence items. Their 09-20 requests share 5 entries and\n    29\t  cite none in common. Across draws, total against CPU shares 0–5%. The SemiAnalysis uplift was filed under Data Center only.\n    30\t- **Unsupported arithmetic:** in 17 of the 24 answers both readers rejected, the figures came from:\n    31\t  - adding amounts of unknown overlap (#36: $25B + $18B);\n    32\t  - another scope's figure scaled by a mismatched ratio (#38: 730/800 × $1.3T);\n    33\t  - a stacked uplift (#44);\n    34\t  - an unsized trim (#48);\n    35\t  - the system's own earlier figure presented as the market's (old-2 v9: $414B; 44 of 2,375 flagged).\n    36\t- **The production check passes them:** six saved answers still pass with a contradictory forecast or an invented reference\n    37\t  substituted. Only a citation outside the request fails (`judging.check_answer`: rung range, ids, pushes, non-empty fields).\n    38\t\n    39\t## The design causes, ranked\n    40\t\n    41\t1. **Answers are prose with one answer-wide citation list.** No figure is tied to its source, and nothing recomputes. This explains\n    42\t   most of the 24.\n    43\t2. **Related questions compute shared quantities separately.** The judging unit is one question, with 0 dependencies in 139\n    44\t   questions. This explains the contradictions.\n    45\t3. **Filing (narrowest question) and the evidence in view (D198) give related questions different inputs.** The previous conclusion\n    46\t   carries figures without provenance, which is the self-made reference.\n    47\t4. **Opening's bands and pull mode amplify a bad figure:** where the boundary sits decides when the error shows.\n    48\t\n    49\tLinking passed one question's conclusion to another, but not its assumptions. Data Center stopped exceeding the total in the pilot, but\n    50\tthe total added a CPU forecast whose overlap was unresolved (D721).\n    51\t\n    52\t## The converged design (for a new judge version Alex opens)\n    53\t\n    54\t- **One judging call per related family.** Same company and fiscal year, overlapping quantities. Each question keeps its own answer,\n    55\t  and every answer reads from one calculation.\n    56\t- **The judge labels the figures it uses:** what each measures (population, scope, period) and whether it is a source figure, a\n    57\t  calculation or an assumption. Extraction v74i is unchanged.\n    58\t- **Code checks identity and arithmetic only:**\n    59\t  1. a source figure appears in the shown passage it cites;\n    60\t  2. the arithmetic recomputes;\n    61\t  3. a declared part fits within its whole for the same period and scenario;\n    62\t  4. one value per shared quantity, role and scenario across the family;\n    63\t  5. a market reference points to shown external material, or says none.\n    64\t\n    65\t  The model keeps importance: drivers, weights, discounts, and overlap stated as an assumption. A blind reader judges whether an\n    66\t  assumption that crosses a boundary is supported.\n    67\t- **When figures cannot be reconciled, the forecast shows as unresolved,** not as two incompatible answers.\n    68\t- **Bounded to the figures the open questions consume** (D24, D28).\n    69\t- **Families:** declared from stored cases for the test. Production would need a matching version that names the relationship.\n    70\t- **The frozen gold's reasoning is kept:** q01 (upside drivers without a fixed increment), q02 (a segment from the shared total and a\n    71\t  sourced mix), q19 (an execution discount), q22 (FY2028 from q01's base, widened by judgement).\n    72\t\n    73\t## The interim for a first release\n    74\t\n    75\tPublish questions, evidence and events, and show number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the forecast text and its\n    76\thistory withheld together (`bundle.py`).\n    77\t\n    78\t## The one test (registered with the design)\n    79\t\n    80\t- **The $0 gate.** Hand-reconstruct, in the new format:\n    81\t  - old-2 8729/8737, 8734 and 8595, and old-3 9166;\n    82\t  - the four gold controls;\n    83\t  - three planted errors (an amount absent from its quote, a wrong sum, an internal forecast labelled consensus).\n    84\t\n    85\t  The format must expose every defect, represent every control, and fail every plant. Any miss stops the line.\n    86\t- **The paid gate** (Alex's ceiling; 36 calls, about $0.2–0.4 estimated):\n    87\t  - **The arms:** the 09-20 total and Data Center pair in each draw, three samples each, judged jointly and separately under the same\n    88\t    format and checks. Plus three samples each on the O, S and E requests. Every output is read against its source with the arm\n    89\t    hidden.\n    90\t  - **Pass:** the joint arm publishes both answers usable and source-supported in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot,\n    91\t    and at least 3 more usable pairs than the separate arm. Zero published hard contradictions, internal-as-market references, or\n    92\t    unresolved overlap, scope or unsized adjustments that decide the band.\n    93\t  - **Stop:** any such published defect, either coverage line missed, or an incomplete comparison.\n10931:## D724 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 44 converges the code review: keep the v12 launcher refusal and the clean-ups, revert the link-step catch; D723 corrected\n10957:## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n10991:## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\nDESIGN.md\nRESULT.md\nclaude-r45.md\ncodex-r45.md\ncodex-r45.stream\ncodex-r45b.md\ncodex-r45b.stream\ncodex-r46.md\ncodex-r46.stream\nround45-brief.md\nround45b-brief.md\nround46-brief.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3049,3083p;10957,11016p;2476,2483p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; cat .claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3049,3083p;10957,11016p;2476,2483p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; cat .claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md\"","aggregated_output":"## D186 · 2026-10-26 · Asset-thesis rungs describe business outcomes; the favourable end is registered per thesis\n\n- Alex chose option C (\"可以\"): rungs of an asset thesis state the business outcome (above, near or below guidance), and each thesis registers which end is favourable for the company, as a theme thesis's dependants already state a direction. Reason: results and direction separate (NVDA beat four quarters and fell; capital spending can build capacity or hurt returns). Recorded; not implemented in this slice: it changes `check_ladder`, the writer, judging, the UI adapter and the Idea route (value × reader), so it is its own slice with its own measurement.\n\n## D187 · 2026-10-26 · A company's own quantity sits under that company's object, private companies included\n\n- Alex chose option C (\"可以\"): any company's own quantity is a thesis under that company (SpaceX's compute capacity under SpaceX, Alphabet's capital spending under GOOGL), consistent with 06-views rule 5 (\"company figures use the fiscal year\"); a macro theme opens only when a thesis depends on it. Recorded; not implemented in this slice: it needs a private-company object kind in the universe and the one switch (01-universe), its own slice. Until then the gold accepts the Codex reading (evidence to NVDA data-center revenue) for SpaceX.\n\n## D260 · 2026-11-02 · A judgement is a forecast against a reference: the rung the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects; the answer states the reference and the implied outcome (judging-v6)\n\n- Alex, 2026-11-02, asked whether the judge's stance should stay an absolute-band lookup (the current reading) or be judged relative to expectations: \"门槛没有标准，按照你作为 hedge fund analyst 的认识来定\". Decided by Claude under that delegation: the definition below is Claude's analyst judgement, recorded as such, not Alex's words.\n- Mechanism (arm 4 draw 1, all 356 judgements read, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md` §7 and `proof-judging-v6.txt`): 8 of 314 later judgements moved a rung and 320 of 356 reasons say \"remains\"; the FY2027 total revenue question was judged 12 times at neutral while its upward pushes grew from 1 to 35, every reason \"the $392 billion estimate is inside the band … does not establish $400 billion\"; the gross-margin judgement wrote \"leans toward rung 2 but does not warrant moving\"; the 2027 hyperscaler-capex theme stayed below the band management's own forecast names because the forecast \"is not fact\". The judging-v5 prompt asked the judge to \"be precise about what is established\" and said only fact can establish a rung: the model read \"established\" as the bar for leaving a rung and the consensus figure as the anchor. A second cause stays open: the ladder's neutral band is written at opening without naming what it compares against (PRD 06 ladder rule 2 asks for it); that is the extraction's rule and is not changed here.\n- Decided, the analyst's rule: (1) the rung is a forecast, the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. (2) The reference is what the market expects: consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline; a consensus or guidance figure alone keeps the judgement at the reference's rung and, once other evidence has arrived, is never the reason to stay. (3) The judge derives the outcome the evidence implies (reported figures and guidance give a run-rate; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it), checks it against the dependencies' conclusions (a part cannot exceed its whole; a figure spanning several periods or products gives the question only its share), compares it with the rung boundaries and moves when it crosses one. (4) Weight follows tier and novelty: fact fixes what is known; party statements are the strongest forecast input; third-party views and rumours move the forecast in proportion to their specificity; a repeat, another outlet or an opinion with no new fact or calculation moves nothing. (5) The answer states `reference` and `implied_outcome` as required fields from `judging-v6` (`judging.schema_for`; code refuses an empty one; stored beside the rung in `judgements.reference` / `implied_outcome`; a ledger written before v6 gains the columns at its first write), so the D3 stance gold can read the reasoning, not only the rung. Written where the judgement is specified: PRD 06 State rules (`docs/system-design/new-facts.js` STATE_RULES, the generated block) and this record.\n- Proof (`proof-judging-v6.txt`, `proof-judging-v6b.txt`: the last stored judgement request of 14 theses of arm 4 draw 1 re-sent once each under v6 and read beside the stored v5 answers, about a cent): every answer names the reference and derives the implied outcome. Six rungs moved against the stored ones: non-GAAP gross margin 3 → 2 (Q1 reported 75% and Q2 guided 75% sit on the rung-2 boundary), 2027 hyperscaler capex 4 → 5 (management's own \"more than $1 trillion\"), China accelerator share 4 → 5 (share \"fallen to zero\"), China H200 authorization No → Yes (a reported plan to permit named firms and reported progress in reviews, six months before the deadline), Data Center revenue 2 → 3 ($355–360 billion derived from Q1 and the total-revenue proxy, below the $360 billion boundary), Blackwell+Rubin revenue 2 → 1 in the first send by annualising a two-year \"$1 trillion visibility\" figure to $545 billion, a part above its whole: clause (3)'s consistency check was added for it and the re-send gives rung 2 ($320–360 billion, a share of the Data Center segment). Total revenue stays at 3 with the arithmetic shown (H1 $172.6 billion from Q1 and the Q2 guide; $400 billion needs more than $227 billion in H2). Prompt 2,453 → 3,782 characters: the request defined neither what a rung means nor a reference and its \"established\" wording forced the defect; the two sentences that carried it were cut. Configuration `poc-v90` (poc-v89 with judging-v6); the default stays `poc-v69`. Tests: `tests/test_stance_fields.py`. Measured by re-sent stored requests, not by an arm (Alex: \"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\").\n\n## D261 · 2026-11-02 · A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again\n\n- Alex, 2026-11-02, while the judgement ruler (D3) was being built: \"你的尺子做出来和金标真的不能再动了，已经造成了3天的各种漂移，非常的严重，我需要你记录到我们的决策和原则里面，我们做完的review过的尺子金标不能再动了\".\n- The drift he names, counted: the extraction ruler went from the first standard (D229, 2026-10-29) to the signed page version 3 (D243, the same day) to version 5 (D250, 2026-10-31), the gold was re-derived from version 3 to version 5 with 62 recorded changes, and every score between D248 and 2026-10-31 had been read against the version-3 gold (the \"假的测量\" of 2026-10-31); the judgement step had no ruler at all until today. Three days of numbers that cannot be compared with each other.\n- Decided (his words; written at the decision it governs, AGENTS §7.1): once a ruler and its gold have been reviewed (readers who did not write them read them against the decisions; Alex signed), neither the definition nor the gold changes again. A defect found later is a dated correction record beside the gold (`corrections-*.json`), printed with every score and never merged in. A new definition is a new version that only his decision opens, with its own gold derived from scratch; old scores stay as they were and are never compared with the new. A ruler under construction is edited only until that review, and nothing is scored against it before.\n- What is locked by this record: the extraction standard page (`docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`, version 3 signed D243, with D250's four boundaries and counting unit) and `golden-v5/` (sha256 in `golden-v5.sha256`): no version 6; the loop's desk ruler (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/README.md`, D1–D3). What is still under construction and locks at his review: the judgement ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md`, its reader brief, question list and gold `gold-v1.json` (the sign-off is a separate record).\n\n## D262 · 2026-11-02 · The judgement ruler (D3) and its gold are fixed: the gold is reader B's answers; frozen at sha256 636c056d1e4252fa…\n\n- Alex, 2026-11-02, after reading the two readers' reasoning on every disagreement (readers A and B differed on 3 of 23 questions by range or yes/no and on 12 of 20 direction labels; the system disagreed with the draft on the total revenue and Vera CPU questions in every draw): \"那就不要理A了；我们就go with B 好吧，定下尺子金表\".\n- Fixed by that decision: the ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md` (unit: a gold question at the window end 2026-07-14; material: golden-v5's 309 items by sha; a numeric question agrees when the gold's implied range overlaps the band of the rung the judge chose, a yes/no question when the answers match; the two null baselines printed with every score); the question list and the must_open mapping as built (`questions-v1.json`, 22 seeds + the Ohio guarantee); the gold `gold-v1.json` = reader B's 23 answers verbatim (B: a fresh-context Claude reader, model-authored, 3 questions marked no material: CoWoS capacity, semiconductor growth, SK Telecom), sha256 `636c056d1e4252fa759660803067e6ccd67a81067b012905e918aa9dec4005f2` in `gold-v1.sha256` and in `score_judgement.py`, which refuses any other. Reader A (Codex) stays beside it as the control record (`reader-A.json`, `reconcile-v1.md`): its distance from B is the stick's own noise. Claude's two proposals of the afternoon (a three-level score when readers split; toss-up questions excluded) were not adopted: one range per question, every question counts. From here D261 applies: nothing in the ruler or the gold changes; a defect is a dated record in `corrections-v1.json`.\n- First measurement on the frozen gold (`score-r4-identity.txt`, arm 4, three draws, judging-v5): judged questions agreeing 13/19, 15/18, 12/17; the lookup baseline (the rung containing the gold's reference figure) 9/15, 8/14, 8/14; always-neutral 5/11, 5/10, 5/10. Disagreeing in every draw: FY2027 total revenue (gold $400–435 billion, judge neutral by consensus lookup) and Vera CPU revenue (gold $8–18 billion, judge the top rung on management's $20 billion at face value); in two of three: the financing-commitments total (gold $25–60 billion, judge $10–20 billion). Never judged in any draw: NVIDIA's own capex (q12); the operating margin in two draws (q10): evidence never reached them, counted apart as \"no judgement\". The new judge (`judging-v6`, D260) has no run to score yet; a run on `poc-v90` is Alex's call.\n\n## D263 · 2026-11-02 · The judge is written to the frozen gold's own reasoning (judging-v7, poc-v91); a gap to the gold is closed in the judge, not re-measured\n\n- Alex, after the first score on the frozen gold was reported as the system being \"wrong\" on some questions: \"不是啊什么叫错？我不是和你说了就按照claude的标准来就好了嘛\". The gold is Claude's (reader B's) standard by D262; a disagreement is the distance between the judge and that standard, to be closed in the judge's rule, not a verdict to be measured again.\n- What reader B does that judging-v6 did not, read from B's answers on the questions that differed (`judgement-gold/reconcile-v1.md`, `gold-v1.json`): carries the guided growth forward rather than annualising the last quarter flat (Data Center, total revenue); discounts a management target for a product with no shipments by default (Vera CPU: two selling quarters, four million units at $5,000, the company's own choice of another CPU); sizes an announced but unsized commitment from its disclosed comparable (the Firmus backstop from Sharon's); derives a figure no one states from the accounting identities in the evidence (capex from operating less free cash flow); keeps linked conclusions consistent (China share against the H200 authorization theme). Written into `judging-v7.txt` as five clauses (v6 3,782 → 4,924 characters; reason: each clause is a behaviour of the frozen standard the judge lacked), named by `poc-v91`; schema and code unchanged.\n- Proof on the stored requests of the questions whose arm-4 judgement differed from the gold (`proof-judging-v7a.txt`, `proof-judging-v7.txt`; one send each, cents): total revenue rung 3 → 2 (about $421 billion from the guided growth on FY2026's base; gold $400–435 billion), Data Center 3 → 2 (about $372 billion; gold $370–400 billion), Vera CPU 1 → 2 ($12 to below $20 billion, the target discounted for the volume not in hand; gold $8–18 billion), DRAM prices 3 → 2 (about +15%; gold +10–35%), financing total stays 4 ($33.5–39.8 billion; gold $25–60 billion), the Ohio guarantee stays Yes; China share stays below 1% in draw 1, consistent with that draw's H200 theme judged No (the gold has the authorization likely and the share 1–8%; the consistency clause ties the share to the theme, so it moves with it). Six of the seven re-sent questions now land in the gold's band; the end-to-end agreement under judging-v7 needs a run on `poc-v91`, which is Alex's call. A placement gap seen on the way: the Vera CPU question never held the fall-launch statement (filed under the Rubin launch questions), so the judge could not count selling quarters from evidence; the default-discount clause covers it, the filing is a D2 class to count.\n\n## D264 · 2026-11-02 · The extraction reads the day's open questions with their takes lines and files the statements itself (extraction v72, poc-v92): the one-decider architecture Alex chose is built and measured against poc-v91 on the frozen ruler\n\n- Alex, 2026-11-02 evening, after asking why the open library was never adopted as the extraction's context (\"你为什么架构上没有采纳我说的开的库作为step 2 context\"; the answer traced the chain from his 10-31 instruction through the one-draw v82 replay I judged \"不采用\" myself to the D256 proposal left waiting): \"我们非常专注的验证这个架构选择：我们有金标和尺子frozen可以比；我们这个架构设计的核心就是透过适当的Prompt 和引入已经开的题，和题的叙述来决定抽取；现在最新的prompt有修改了很多小毛病，你看是不是用最新最好的prompt + v72这边告诉模型怎么用读取开题库的prompt 来做新的实验prompt。充分理解我的ask然后get it worked out\". This is his choice of the one-decider architecture (review-2026-11-02.md §4 way (i), the D256 proposal) and of its base prompt.\n- Built (design: `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/design-v72.md`, the four tables of AGENTS §2, predictions frozen at sha256 `aec1bb40…` in `predictions-v72.sha256` before any send): extraction version 72, named by `poc/config/poc-v92.json` (= poc-v91 with T*-v72 and no placement setting). The request shows the questions open at the start of the item's day (D251's snapshot) each with the code-written takes line the placer read (`placement.question_lines`, one writer for both requests); the schema defines the evidence field `links` by the same rule (`placement.FILING_RULE`, the placer's v4 system-prompt rule restated beside the field: the narrowest open question whose takes line covers the statement, whoever says it, with or without a period or amount, plus the answer's own candidates, else empty); `role-v72.txt` is `role-v66.txt` with its first paragraph pointing at [Open questions] and the links field (the latest extraction prompt on the frozen extraction gold: v53 → v65 gold-rejected kept per draw about 109 → 59 with core and supporting flat, v66 = v65 + R3's boundary, `r3-final-scores-Y6.txt`); `categories-v72.json` and `review-v72.txt` are v66's. The extraction's links file each statement: one linked to an open question is filed there, one linked only to its candidates follows them, one linked to nothing is dropped as 'no home' (D209; the handover's reason is the same word, so `e2e_funnel` and `dropped_census` read it); no placement call exists for v72 (`extraction.one_decider`, `places` ends at v71). v71's `new_in_it` and `moves` fields are not asked (`MOVES_FIELDS_VERSIONS`). Settled by me under the delegation of 2026-11-01, and said so: the candidate rules stay v66's (propose when the item raises it; code owns identity and folds a duplicate of an open question, D258), not v71's \"only for a matter no open question covers\", which halved the candidates and the homes in v82; it is one sentence to tighten if the questions ruler says so.\n- Two wirings of D251's snapshot were wrong and are fixed in the same change, each with a test that fails on its mutant (`tests/test_one_decider.py`): (1) before the first completed day the snapshot was empty, so the seeds (seq 0, D253) were invisible to every first-day item while the placer of poc-v91 saw them (`store.day_start_seq` is 0 before the first completed day); (2) the takes line prints a question's group names and aliases, which D257's alias merges change within a day, so the request bytes would have changed mid-day, the parallel day would have re-sent every waiting request, and two items of one day would have seen different lists (`store.groups_of_view_at` reads memberships and aliases at the snapshot's seq). Version gates: v53's and v71's request bytes are unchanged (tests); 274 tests pass; `scripts/preflight.py` over arm 4 draw 1 replays 243 stored answers through the current checks with the same 22 refusals as before (`preflight-v72-prep.txt`).\n- Proof before the run (cents; `harness/resend_extract_v72.py`, `proof-v72-links.txt`: the four rack-delay articles of 2026-07-05/06 rebuilt under v72 from arm 4 draw 1's day-start snapshots, three sends each; the stored outcome of the same run as the control). The statements that name nothing (\"Our roadmap is intact\", the scrapped backup plan, NVL72x2 back-to-back racks), which the placer dropped or filed under same-day duplicate questions in every arm since 10-31, are filed under the seed question v18 (Rubin Ultra / Kyber NVL144 shipping) in 3/3 sends of the SemiAnalysis article (both statements), 3/3 of the Tom's Hardware article (NVL72x2; the denial 2/3 with one send's quote refused), 3/3 of the Cramer article (to v18, v2 or v31 by send), while in the Asian-suppliers article the NVL72x2 statement went once to no home and twice to the revenue questions (v1/v2, v2/v20: a sink link; the Kyber question v33 the control's placer used was opened that same day and is outside the snapshot). Zero candidates in 27 sends over nine matched articles against the control's four, all four Kyber duplicates of v18 (the list shown does the deduplication the matching step did after the fact). Request size 22–38K characters (27–44 open questions) against the control's mean 19.8K.\n- The measurement, launched 2026-11-02 18:05 at his \"get it worked out\": `arms/r6-one-decider-v92/d1..3` against `arms/r6-control-v91/d1..3` (the acceptance run he stopped at 17:27, now the control, since arm 4 and v92 are separated by D258, D259 and D263 as well), 2026-07-01..14, seeds v2, eight extraction workers each, cap $3 a draw; scored on the frozen ruler (`e2e_funnel.py`, `score_judgement.py`), regressions first, every number, in `log.md` row 12 and `design-v72.md` §8. Whether poc-v92 becomes the default is his call after the numbers.\n- Measured (six draws finished 19:40; `e2e-funnel-r6-v72.txt`, `judgement-gold/score-r6-*`, `matter-states-r6-v72.txt`, `probe-v72-sink.txt`; three-draw means, v91 → v92). Regressions first: core matters reaching judgement 76.3 → 73.7 of 86 (predicted ≥ +2, the null is ±2), core dropped for no home 4.0 → 5.7, article-opened questions 11.7 → 3.0 (candidates 65 → 6.7: the list shown suppresses proposals even with the candidate rule unchanged; must_open 28/28 and may_open 40/42 in both arms because the seeds cover them, the Ohio guarantee being the one visible loss), supporting not extracted 25.3 → 46.0. Held: supporting reaching 94.0 → 90.0 (at the −4 line), noise reaching 89.2 → 56.9 (−36%), judgement agreement 17/19, 17/18, 17/19 → 15/18, 16/17, 17/18 against lookup 8–9/14–15, cost $1.15 → $0.88 a draw with model time −36% and wall clock 95 → 46 minutes for three draws, zero re-sent requests. Two mechanisms, both in sentences and neither in the architecture: (1) the sink is back: 60–62% of links on the three company-wide revenue questions against v91's 34–40%, 190–208 statements a draw under both total and Data Center revenue against 5–6; the model's own account in three of three cases cites the figure-line takes clause D259 added (\"what makes that figure more or less likely: the demand, supply, competition and pricing behind it\") and concedes the links field's \"narrowest only\" should have excluded the broader question or the link altogether; (2) role-v66's end-of-request check removes 21 supporting matters a draw that v53 keeps (20 matters extracted in v91 in at least two draws and in v92 in at most one: third parties' actions and views, named hires and partners, product milestones, standard §5.1 kinds 2–3), a loss the extraction bench's \"supporting in at least two draws\" count had hidden. Verdict: as built, v72 is neither better nor worse than v91 on the desk's counts and is cleaner, cheaper and faster; it does not become the default and no further arm is sent before the two mechanisms are fixed at their owners with $0 proofs: the root/driver pair collapsed to the narrower question by code (identity, D207's rule), the figure-line clause reworded and proved on re-sent stored v92 requests, and the base text (v53 against v66 under the architecture) put to Alex.\n\n## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n\n- **Alex's words** (2026-11-22): \"work with counsel and have a look at the traces of this problem … what is wrong with the system design\n  overall … look at the code, look at the traces, deeply battle it out with counsel … because I think it's the most important thing\n  that we don't hallucinate with the numbers, and I want you to get this right\".\n- **The record:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/` (`RESULT.md`).\n  - Claude's reflection was written before Codex's.\n  - Codex ran an independent investigation (fresh thread `01a20501…`) and a challenge round.\n  - Consensus. One wording point stays open: the $146B is arithmetically a residual, but the order of the judge's choices is unknown.\n- **Diagnosis:**\n  1. Answers are prose; code ties no figure to a source and recomputes nothing. The production check passes contradictory or invented\n     figures.\n  2. Related questions compute the same quantities separately. The unit is one question, with 0 dependencies.\n  3. Filing and the evidence in view split their inputs. The previous conclusion carries figures without provenance.\n  4. Opening's bands amplify an error.\n- **Measured:**\n  - Data Center Q4 above company Q4 on at least 13 of 26 days in old-1;\n  - Data Center's full year above the total's on 20 consecutive days in old-2;\n  - different Q3 bases on 17 of 18 paired days;\n  - shared evidence between total and Data Center 8% in old-2;\n  - 17 of the 24 double-rejected answers from unchecked arithmetic.\n- **Recommended design** (a new judge version, Alex's to open):\n  - one judging call per related family, each question keeping its answer from one calculation;\n  - figures labelled by the judge (source, calculation, assumption; scope and period);\n  - code checks only identity and arithmetic (figure in quote, recompute, part within whole, one value per shared quantity, a sourced\n    reference);\n  - unreconciled forecasts shown as unresolved;\n  - extraction unchanged;\n  - families declared for the test.\n- **Interim for a first release:** number questions shown as \"Forecast unavailable\" until they pass the checks.\n- **The test:** a $0 gate (hand reconstructions of five stored cases, four gold controls, three planted errors), then a paid gate\n  (36 calls; joint against separate on the three draws' 09-20 pair, plus O, S and E singletons). Pass and stop lines are in `RESULT.md`.\n- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\n\n## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n\n- **The questions** (after D725):\n  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n  - \"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\" Options: 同意\n    (recommended); 暂不定.\n- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\"; \"同意 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex):**\n  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\n    ceiling.\n  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the\n    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\n- poc-v118 stays the product.\n---\nname: prompt-audit\ndescription: After every measurement of an extraction configuration, and before any prompt change, map each failure class in the stored draws to the sentence of the request that produced it, check that sentence against the frozen standard and the prompt principles, and write the audit table. Alex, 2026-11-02 - \"你应该看着prompt，然后对比失败的trace，然后仔细的根据尺子做对比，并且我们prompt的principle也要带入，是尝试教他general hedge fund analyst skill，不是要hardcode或是benchmark farming；你把这个写成一个skill以后固定跑\".\n---\n\n# Prompt audit: failures → the request's sentences → the standard → the principle\n\nRun this after every measured configuration (three draws scored on the frozen ruler) and before any edit to a prompt file, a schema\ndescription or a takes line. A measurement without this audit is a score without a diagnosis (AGENTS §7.2, §6). The audit is read,\nnot scripted: the scripts below only produce the lists to read.\n\n## 0. Inputs\n\n- The arm's run folders (`docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/arms/<arm>/d1..3`) and the baseline's.\n- The frozen ruler (AGENTS §7.1): the extraction standard `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html` (version 3, D243, with D250's\n  boundaries), golden-v5, the questions standard, the judgement gold. Never edited; every disagreement is a gap in the system.\n- The prompt principles (AGENTS §6 and §8): the prompt carries the standard and no new rule; it teaches a general hedge-fund\n  analyst, so every sentence and example reads the same for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip maker, names no covered\n  company, product or number, and takes no example from a test article; a classification is a closed set with examples; never grow a\n  prompt to fix quality without cutting as much elsewhere; a field's definition sits in the schema beside the field; code owns\n  identity, never importance.\n\n## 1. Dump the request as the model reads it\n\nOne stored request of the configuration (any article), printed whole: the system text (the role), every user block before the item\n(category block, subjects, research reference, open questions with their takes lines, research groups), the closing sentence, the\nend-of-request check, and every schema field description (evidence and candidates). Read it top to bottom once. List every\ninstruction that decides keep, reject, link, open, or a field value, with its location (role paragraph, check row, schema field,\ntakes line, category block). This list is the thing the failures are mapped onto.\n\n```sh\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport sqlite3, json\na = sqlite3.connect('file:<run folder>/archive.sqlite?mode=ro', uri=True)\nreq = json.loads(a.execute(\"select request_json from model_calls where purpose='extract' and request_json like '%<title fragment>%' order by call_id desc limit 1\").fetchone()[0])\nprint(req['messages'][0]['content']); print(req['messages'][1]['content'].split('[Item]')[0]); print(req['messages'][1]['content'].rsplit('\\n\\n', 2)[-2:])\nprint(json.dumps({k: v.get('description') for k, v in req['response_format']['json_schema']['schema']['properties']['evidence']['items']['properties'].items() if v.get('description')}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))\nPY\n```\n\n## 2. Produce the failure lists (all at no model cost, on the stored draws)\n\n| List | Script | What it gives |\n|---|---|---|\n| Matter states across draws | `harness/matter_states.py arm=d1,d2,d3 base=d1,d2,d3` | every gold core/supporting matter: extracted or reaching in 3/2/1/0 draws; the systematic misses (0 of 3) and the coin flips (1 of 3) |\n| Written noise by the standard's row | the `rows_all` count in `design-v72.md` §10 (the gold's `not_kept[].row`) | which row of the standard the written noise falls under, with examples |\n| No-home drops | `harness/dropped_census.py d1 d2 d3` | gold matters written but dropped, with the questions open at the time |\n| Where links go | `harness/links_by_question.py d1 d2 d3 --sample 20` | the pile per question, the revenue-sink share, statements under several questions, noise under revenue |\n| Quote refusals | the `dropped` reasons of the handovers (`quote not in item`), each diffed against its closest source window | paraphrase against a word or two off |\n| Question recall | `harness/question_recall.py d1 d2 d3` | must_open / may_open covered by seeds and by article-opened questions |\n| Fields | 15 random stored statements with speaker, original_who, original_day, tier | read against the quote and the item's day and publisher |\n\nFor every list, read the items, not the counts: the raw answer beside the article for every systematic miss (a miss the scorer reports\nmay be the matter written in other words: check before counting it), a sample of twenty for every pile.\n\n## 3. Map each failure class to the request\n\nFor each class with more than a handful of cases, fill one row:\n\n| Failure class (count, share) | The sentence(s) of the request that produced it, quoted | The standard's line on the same case (section, decision) | Verdict | The model's own account (when the sentence is not obvious) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n\nVerdicts, one of: **contradiction** (two sentences of the request pull opposite ways, or a request sentence removes what the standard\nkeeps, D240), **missing** (no sentence decides the case; the model guesses, a coin flip per send), **abstract** (a clause without an\nexample, read differently each send), **misread** (the sentence is right, the model does not apply it; needs the model's own account\nbefore any change), **not the prompt** (code, scorer or sampler).\n\nThe model's own account: continue the stored conversation with one question about one case (`harness/probe_v72_link.py`,\n`probe_v72_missing.py`), a cent a case, for every \"misread\" and for any class whose sentence is not obvious from reading.\n\n## 4. Check every proposed fix against the principles before writing it\n\n- It is written from the standard's line, not from the failing article: the example comes from another domain, names no covered\n  company, product or number, and reads the same for every industry. A fix that only recovers the bench's misses is benchmark\n  farming and is not written.\n- It removes a contradiction, supplies a missing definition at its owner (schema field, takes line, check row, category block), or\n  replaces an abstract clause with a closed set and examples. It never adds a rule the standard does not hold.\n- It cuts at least as much as it adds, or the growth has a written reason; report characters before and after.\n- One class per change; the change is proved on the stored requests of that class, three sends as stored against three changed,\n  with the noise guards of the same articles; the whole bench accepts it (three draws) only when Alex asks for a run.\n\n## 5. Output\n\nWrite the table and the verdicts into the arm's design document (a numbered section), one row per class, in the order of the loss;\nthe report to Alex states each class in a reader's words (what the system does wrong, which sentence makes it do that, what the\nstandard says), never in the loop's own words (AGENTS, \"Authority and scope\": explain as to a sixteen-year-old).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt; rg -n 'def check_answer|def evidence_shown_in|def request_parts|def _record' src/hivemind/views/judging.py; rg -n 'def answer_shape|def view_bundle' src/hivemind/bundle.py; rg -n 'mean|interval|intersect|overlap' docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/{ruler-v1.md,score_judgement.py}\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt; rg -n 'def check_answer|def evidence_shown_in|def request_parts|def _record' src/hivemind/views/judging.py; rg -n 'def answer_shape|def view_bundle' src/hivemind/bundle.py; rg -n 'mean|interval|intersect|overlap' docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/{ruler-v1.md,score_judgement.py}\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging a thesis's current rung. Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes in force. The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n     2\t\n     3\t- Rejudge from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently), the current conclusions of dependencies and the themes in force. Pieces in force that no recent judgement relied on are not shown; the previous conclusion carries them. Do not add to or subtract from the previous score. The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison.\n     4\t- Judge against a reference: what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on the ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     6\t- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n     7\t- “Themes in force” lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on this thesis and report it in theme_pushes with the direction it pushes this thesis (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked “updated since this thesis was last judged” may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     8\t- A dependency marked “not yet created” supplies no input. A dependency marked “historical only” is closed without a successor; its closing conclusion is background only.\n     9\t- Your conclusion must be consistent with the conclusions of the theses it depends on and the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open; a component cannot exceed its whole.\n    10\t- Return the rung's one-based position; reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n    11\t- changed is true for a different rung or a change to the key facts or figures supporting the same rung, including a changed implied outcome. Repetition or another source for the same statement does not alone change the conclusion. The first judgement always has changed true.\n225:def request_parts(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n253:def evidence_shown_in(request_text):\n259:def check_answer(conn, view_id, data, request_text=None, lists=None):\n306:def _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer):\n82:def answer_shape(views_db, view_id):\n100:def view_bundle(views_db, item_of, view_id, as_of=None):\ndocs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/score_judgement.py:2:question agrees when the gold's implied range overlaps the band of the rung the judge chose, a yes/no question when the answers match.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json; b=\\\"docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/\\\"; d=json.load(open(b+\\\"gold-v1.json\\\")); ss=json.load(open(\\\"poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json\\\")); p=json.load(open(b+\\\"packet-v1.json\\\")); print(type(ss),list(ss)[:2] if type(ss)==dict else str(ss[0])[:120]); print(type(p),list(p)[:4] if type(p)==dict else str(p[0])[:120]); ids=(\\\"q01\\\",\\\"q02\\\",\\\"q19\\\",\\\"q22\\\"); print(json.dumps([e for e in d[\\\"entries\\\"] if e[\\\"question_id\\\"] in ids],indent=2))' \"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json; b=\\\"docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/\\\"; d=json.load(open(b+\\\"gold-v1.json\\\")); ss=json.load(open(\\\"poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json\\\")); p=json.load(open(b+\\\"packet-v1.json\\\")); print(type(ss),list(ss)[:2] if type(ss)==dict else str(ss[0])[:120]); print(type(p),list(p)[:4] if type(p)==dict else str(p[0])[:120]); ids=(\\\"q01\\\",\\\"q02\\\",\\\"q19\\\",\\\"q22\\\"); print(json.dumps([e for e in d[\\\"entries\\\"] if e[\\\"question_id\\\"] in ids],indent=2))' \"","aggregated_output":"<class 'dict'> ['company', 'as_of']\n<class 'dict'> ['ruler_version', 'about', 'gold_sha256', 'items']\n[\n  {\n    \"question_id\": \"q01\",\n    \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n    \"kind\": \"asset\",\n    \"unit\": \"USD\",\n    \"seed_view_id\": \"v1\",\n    \"source\": \"reader B\",\n    \"no_view\": false,\n    \"reference\": {\n      \"text\": \"Wall Street consensus $392bn for this fiscal year (i037), consistent with the 82% growth analysts project for this year (i090, i174).\",\n      \"value\": 392000000000,\n      \"items\": [\n        \"i037\",\n        \"i090\",\n        \"i174\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"implied_outcome\": {\n      \"text\": \"Q1 actual $81.6bn (i280) plus Q2 guidance $91bn plus or minus 2% (i281) give $172.6bn for the first half, so consensus needs about $219bn in the second half. Management says growth rates are accelerating as quarterly revenue approaches $100bn (i295); SemiAnalysis tracks second-half data-center compute 20% above consensus and shipment volumes materially above market estimates (i106, i208, i111); Rubin first shipments are scheduled for Q3 2026 with a volume ramp in Q4 (i219, i105) at about double the GB300 rack price (i216); management targets $20bn of Vera CPU sales by fiscal year-end (i288). A second half of $228-262bn gives $400-435bn.\",\n      \"low\": 400000000000,\n      \"high\": 435000000000,\n      \"yes_no\": null,\n      \"items\": [\n        \"i280\",\n        \"i281\",\n        \"i295\",\n        \"i106\",\n        \"i219\",\n        \"i216\",\n        \"i288\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"direction\": \"above\",\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n    \"decisive_items\": [\n      \"i281\",\n      \"i295\",\n      \"i106\",\n      \"i219\",\n      \"i037\"\n    ],\n    \"against\": {\n      \"text\": \"Unnamed reports of delays across the upcoming Vera Rubin server lineup (i133); the Kyber report leaves 2026 Rubin on the Oberon rack untouched (i202), but memory stays tight until 2028 (i252) and the guidance assumes no China data-center compute revenue (i281).\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"i133\",\n        \"i252\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"reasoning\": \"The Street expects $392bn for FY2027 (i037), which is the 82% growth analysts project (i090). The known half is $172.6bn: Q1 revenue $81.6bn (i280) plus Q2 guidance of $91bn plus or minus 2% (i281), so consensus needs about $219bn in the second half. Management told a Morgan Stanley roadshow that growth rates are accelerating as quarterly revenue approaches $100bn (i295), and SemiAnalysis tracks second-half data-center compute 20% above consensus with shipment volumes materially above market estimates (i106, i208, i111). Rubin ships from Q3 2026 with the volume ramp in Q4 (i219, i105) at about $7.8m a rack against $4m for GB300 (i216), and management targets $20bn of Vera CPU sales by fiscal year-end (i288). A second half of $228-262bn gives $400-435bn, above consensus. The risks are supply, with memory tight until 2028 (i252), rumoured delays across the Vera Rubin lineup (i133), and guidance that assumes no China data-center compute revenue (i281).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question_id\": \"q02\",\n    \"question\": \"What Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n    \"kind\": \"asset\",\n    \"unit\": \"USD\",\n    \"seed_view_id\": \"v2\",\n    \"source\": \"reader B\",\n    \"no_view\": false,\n    \"reference\": {\n      \"text\": \"No segment consensus is stated; consensus total revenue of $392bn (i037) at the Q1 Data Center share of 92% of sales (i129) implies about $360bn.\",\n      \"value\": 360000000000,\n      \"items\": [\n        \"i037\",\n        \"i129\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"implied_outcome\": {\n      \"text\": \"Q1 Data Center $75.25bn (i129, i151); Q2 total guided $91bn (i281) at the same share is about $84bn, so the first half is roughly $159bn. My total-revenue view of $400-435bn (q01: i295, i106, i219) at a 92-93% share, with SemiAnalysis expecting second-half data-center compute 20% above consensus (i106, i208), gives $370-400bn.\",\n      \"low\": 370000000000,\n      \"high\": 400000000000,\n      \"yes_no\": null,\n      \"items\": [\n        \"i129\",\n        \"i151\",\n        \"i281\",\n        \"i106\",\n        \"i208\",\n        \"i295\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"direction\": \"above\",\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n    \"decisive_items\": [\n      \"i129\",\n      \"i281\",\n      \"i106\",\n      \"i208\",\n      \"i295\"\n    ],\n    \"against\": {\n      \"text\": \"Unnamed reports of delays across the Vera Rubin server lineup (i133); the guidance assumes zero China data-center compute revenue (i281, i156).\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"i133\",\n        \"i281\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"reasoning\": \"No segment consensus is stated; the Street's $392bn total (i037) at the Q1 Data Center share of 92% of sales (i129) implies about $360bn. Q1 Data Center was $75.25bn, up 92% year on year and 21% quarter on quarter (i129, i151), and Q2 guidance of $91bn (i281) at the same share is about $84bn, so the first half is roughly $159bn. SemiAnalysis expects second-half data-center compute 20% above the Street (i106, i208), management describes accelerating growth toward $100bn quarters (i295), and Rubin volume ramps in Q4 at nearly twice the rack price (i219, i216). My total-revenue view of $400-435bn at a 92-93% share gives $370-400bn, above the implied consensus. The guidance assumes zero China data-center compute (i281, i156), so any H200 permission (i270) is upside not in these numbers; the rumoured Vera Rubin lineup delays (i133) are the downside.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question_id\": \"q19\",\n    \"question\": \"How much revenue will NVIDIA report from standalone Vera CPUs in FY2027?\",\n    \"kind\": \"asset\",\n    \"unit\": \"USD\",\n    \"seed_view_id\": \"v19\",\n    \"source\": \"reader B\",\n    \"no_view\": false,\n    \"reference\": {\n      \"text\": \"Management's own figure: $20bn of stand-alone CPU sales this year (i095), by the end of this fiscal year (i288), nearly $20bn with no period (i080): one claim retold three times.\",\n      \"value\": 20000000000,\n      \"items\": [\n        \"i288\",\n        \"i095\",\n        \"i080\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"implied_outcome\": {\n      \"text\": \"The first stand-alone CPU launches this fall (i096), so the revenue falls in roughly two quarters; at Morgan Stanley's $5,000 per Vera CPU (i218), $20bn is four million units. Demand signals are real: Perplexity plans to deploy Vera in production (i262, i291) and Intel's CEO sees the CPU:GPU ratio in inference moving toward 1:1 (i009); but NVIDIA chose Intel Xeon 6 as host CPU for DGX Rubin NVL8 (i008). I bet $8-18bn, below the $20bn ambition.\",\n      \"low\": 8000000000,\n      \"high\": 18000000000,\n      \"yes_no\": null,\n      \"items\": [\n        \"i096\",\n        \"i218\",\n        \"i262\",\n        \"i291\",\n        \"i009\",\n        \"i008\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"direction\": \"below\",\n    \"confidence\": \"low\",\n    \"decisive_items\": [\n      \"i288\",\n      \"i095\",\n      \"i096\",\n      \"i218\"\n    ],\n    \"against\": {\n      \"text\": \"Management expects $20bn by fiscal year-end (i288, i095), and Intel's CEO describes inference moving toward one CPU per GPU (i009).\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"i288\",\n        \"i009\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"reasoning\": \"The reference is management's own number: $20bn of stand-alone CPU sales this year (i095), by the end of this fiscal year (i288), nearly $20bn with no period (i080), one claim retold three times. The first stand-alone CPU launches this fall (i096), so the revenue falls in roughly two quarters, and at Morgan Stanley's $5,000 per Vera CPU (i218) $20bn is four million units. Demand signals are real: Perplexity plans to deploy Vera in production after a 1.5x result on agentic coding (i262, i291), and Intel's CEO sees the CPU:GPU ratio in inference moving from 1:8 toward 1:1 (i009); but NVIDIA itself chose Intel Xeon 6 as host CPU for DGX Rubin NVL8 (i008). Lean cautious on a product with no shipments yet: I bet $8-18bn, below the $20bn ambition, with the top of the range reachable if the fall ramp is steep. Management's $20bn (i288, i095) is the strongest item against.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question_id\": \"q22\",\n    \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2028?\",\n    \"kind\": \"asset\",\n    \"unit\": \"USD\",\n    \"seed_view_id\": \"v22\",\n    \"source\": \"reader B\",\n    \"no_view\": false,\n    \"reference\": {\n      \"text\": \"Wall Street consensus $554bn (i037), the 41% growth analysts project for next year (i090, i174).\",\n      \"value\": 554000000000,\n      \"items\": [\n        \"i037\",\n        \"i090\",\n        \"i174\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"implied_outcome\": {\n      \"text\": \"A higher FY2027 base of $400-435bn (q01: i295, i106) at the Street's 41% (i090) is $565-615bn; NVIDIA projects the big four's capex rising from $650bn to over $1 trillion in 2027 (i256, i173), a 54% step; Huang's $1 trillion of Blackwell and Rubin sales through 2027 (i079) exceeds consensus total revenue over the window; Rubin racks sell at about twice the GB300 price (i216) and Vera CPUs add a line (i288). Against: the Kyber rack may slip to 2028 (i100) with Oberon-Rubin racks filling the gap (i181), and memory stays tight until 2028 (i252). I bet $560-640bn.\",\n      \"low\": 560000000000,\n      \"high\": 640000000000,\n      \"yes_no\": null,\n      \"items\": [\n        \"i295\",\n        \"i090\",\n        \"i256\",\n        \"i079\",\n        \"i216\",\n        \"i100\",\n        \"i181\",\n        \"i252\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"direction\": \"above\",\n    \"confidence\": \"low\",\n    \"decisive_items\": [\n      \"i037\",\n      \"i256\",\n      \"i079\",\n      \"i100\"\n    ],\n    \"against\": {\n      \"text\": \"SemiAnalysis's Kyber delay to 2028 with the four-die Rubin Ultra cancelled (i100, i179) pushes the next product step out of FY2028, and Meta's CEO sees slower AI-agent progress (i292).\",\n      \"items\": [\n        \"i100\",\n        \"i292\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"reasoning\": \"Consensus is $554bn (i037), the 41% growth analysts project for next year (i090, i174). A higher FY2027 base of $400-435bn (q01: i295, i106) at the same 41% is $565-615bn. NVIDIA projects the big four's capex rising from $650bn to over $1 trillion in 2027 (i256, i173), a 54% step, Huang's $1 trillion of Blackwell and Rubin sales through 2027 (i079) exceeds consensus total revenue over the window, Rubin racks sell at about twice the GB300 price (i216), and Vera CPUs add a line (i288). Against: SemiAnalysis has the Kyber rack slipping to 2028 with the four-die Rubin Ultra cancelled (i100, i179), which pushes the next product step out of FY2028 and leaves Oberon-Rubin racks to fill it (i181); memory stays tight until 2028 (i252); and Meta's CEO sees slower AI-agent progress (i292). I bet $560-640bn, above consensus, with low confidence eighteen months out.\"\n  }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '10957,11020p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/score_judgement.py | sed -n '1,35p;85,137p'; sed -n '90,106p' AGENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '10957,11020p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/score_judgement.py | sed -n '1,35p;85,137p'; sed -n '90,106p' AGENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"## D725 · 2026-11-22 · Council round 45/45b: the number answers fail because related numbers have no shared, checked calculation; one judge version and one test recommended to Alex\n\n- **Alex's words** (2026-11-22): \"work with counsel and have a look at the traces of this problem … what is wrong with the system design\n  overall … look at the code, look at the traces, deeply battle it out with counsel … because I think it's the most important thing\n  that we don't hallucinate with the numbers, and I want you to get this right\".\n- **The record:** `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/` (`RESULT.md`).\n  - Claude's reflection was written before Codex's.\n  - Codex ran an independent investigation (fresh thread `01a20501…`) and a challenge round.\n  - Consensus. One wording point stays open: the $146B is arithmetically a residual, but the order of the judge's choices is unknown.\n- **Diagnosis:**\n  1. Answers are prose; code ties no figure to a source and recomputes nothing. The production check passes contradictory or invented\n     figures.\n  2. Related questions compute the same quantities separately. The unit is one question, with 0 dependencies.\n  3. Filing and the evidence in view split their inputs. The previous conclusion carries figures without provenance.\n  4. Opening's bands amplify an error.\n- **Measured:**\n  - Data Center Q4 above company Q4 on at least 13 of 26 days in old-1;\n  - Data Center's full year above the total's on 20 consecutive days in old-2;\n  - different Q3 bases on 17 of 18 paired days;\n  - shared evidence between total and Data Center 8% in old-2;\n  - 17 of the 24 double-rejected answers from unchecked arithmetic.\n- **Recommended design** (a new judge version, Alex's to open):\n  - one judging call per related family, each question keeping its answer from one calculation;\n  - figures labelled by the judge (source, calculation, assumption; scope and period);\n  - code checks only identity and arithmetic (figure in quote, recompute, part within whole, one value per shared quantity, a sourced\n    reference);\n  - unreconciled forecasts shown as unresolved;\n  - extraction unchanged;\n  - families declared for the test.\n- **Interim for a first release:** number questions shown as \"Forecast unavailable\" until they pass the checks.\n- **The test:** a $0 gate (hand reconstructions of five stored cases, four gold controls, three planted errors), then a paid gate\n  (36 calls; joint against separate on the three draws' 09-20 pair, plus O, S and E singletons). Pass and stop lines are in `RESULT.md`.\n- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\n\n## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n\n- **The questions** (after D725):\n  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n  - \"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\" Options: 同意\n    (recommended); 暂不定.\n- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\"; \"同意 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex):**\n  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\n    ceiling.\n  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the\n    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\n- poc-v118 stays the product.\n     1\t\"\"\"D3, the judgement score (ruler-v1.md §1): for each gold question, the run's last judgement on or before the window end; a numeric\n     2\tquestion agrees when the gold's implied range overlaps the band of the rung the judge chose, a yes/no question when the answers match.\n     3\tPrints every question, the totals, the two null baselines (the rung containing the gold's reference figure; always the neutral rung) and\n     4\tthe gold's own reader-disagreement count. Refuses a gold whose sha256 or ruler version is not the one written here (D261).\n     5\t\n     6\t    python3 score_judgement.py <run folder> [--day 2026-07-14] [--map q23=v25 ...]\n     7\t\"\"\"\n     8\timport argparse\n     9\timport hashlib\n    10\timport json\n    11\timport sqlite3\n    12\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    13\t\n    14\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    15\tRULER_VERSION = 1\n    16\tGOLD_SHA256 = '636c056d1e4252fa759660803067e6ccd67a81067b012905e918aa9dec4005f2'   # frozen 2026-11-02 (D262); gold-v1.sha256 holds the same value\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\tdef main():\n    20\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    21\t    ap.add_argument('run'); ap.add_argument('--day', default='2026-07-14'); ap.add_argument('--map', nargs='*', default=[])\n    22\t    args = ap.parse_args()\n    23\t    gold_path = HERE / 'gold-v1.json'\n    24\t    sha = hashlib.sha256(gold_path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n    25\t    gold = json.loads(gold_path.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))\n    26\t    if gold.get('ruler_version') != RULER_VERSION:\n    27\t        raise SystemExit(f'gold ruler_version {gold.get(\"ruler_version\")} != scorer {RULER_VERSION}: refused')\n    28\t    frozen = (HERE / 'gold-v1.sha256').read_text().split()[0] if (HERE / 'gold-v1.sha256').exists() else None\n    29\t    if GOLD_SHA256 and frozen != GOLD_SHA256:\n    30\t        raise SystemExit(f'gold-v1.sha256 {frozen} != the frozen value in this scorer {GOLD_SHA256}: refused')\n    31\t    if frozen and frozen != sha:\n    32\t        raise SystemExit(f'gold sha256 {sha} != frozen {frozen}: refused')\n    33\t    corrections = json.loads((HERE / 'corrections-v1.json').read_text()) if (HERE / 'corrections-v1.json').exists() else []\n    34\t    label = 'FROZEN' if frozen else f'DRAFT, {gold.get(\"status\")}'\n    35\t    print(f'gold v{RULER_VERSION} sha256 {sha[:16]}… [{label}]; corrections on record, not applied: {len(corrections)}; run {args.run}; window end {args.day}')\n    85\t                neutral = (n['lo'] is None or implied['high'] >= n['lo']) and (n['hi'] is None or implied['low'] < n['hi'])\n    86\t        totals['agree' if agree else 'disagree'] += 1\n    87\t        if lookup is not None:\n    88\t            base_lookup[0] += lookup; base_lookup[1] += 1\n    89\t        if neutral is not None:\n    90\t            base_neutral[0] += neutral; base_neutral[1] += 1\n    91\t        print(f'{qid:<4}{(\"agree\" if agree else \"DISAGREE\"):<14}{gold_text:<28}{(vid + \" rung \" + str(j[\"rung\"]) + \" \" + chosen[\"label\"][:12] + \" \" + band)[:39]:<40}'\n    92\t              f'{(\"\" if lookup is None else (\"yes\" if lookup else \"no\")):<8}{(\"\" if neutral is None else (\"yes\" if neutral else \"no\")):<8}{q[\"question\"][:60]}')\n    93\t    judged = totals['agree'] + totals['disagree']\n    94\t    print(f'\\ntotals: {totals}; agreement {totals[\"agree\"]}/{judged} of judged questions')\n    95\t    print(f'null baselines: the rung containing the gold reference agrees {base_lookup[0]}/{base_lookup[1]}; always neutral agrees {base_neutral[0]}/{base_neutral[1]}')\n    96\t    noise = (gold.get('readers') or {}).get('stick_noise') or {}\n    97\t    print(f'gold = reader B (D262); control reader A differs on {len(noise.get(\"range_or_yesno_disagreements\", []))} questions by range or yes/no and on {len(noise.get(\"direction_label_splits\", []))} direction labels; [{label}]')\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   101\t    main()\n\n## 2. Before writing code: design\n\nCode written before the thinking costs rounds of review. A design holds these tables before code and before any review; a blank cell\nmeans it is not ready:\n\n1. **State × event**, for work that spans more than one step, run or day: every state against every event it can meet (success,\n   refusal, a refused retry, an external failure, a crash midway, work still in flight when a run ends, a later run on a later date,\n   configuration changed in between, an input corrected while waiting, another writer of the same data, two scopes at once), including\n   the work before its first step and after its terminal outcome. Each cell names the transition, what is written, and the date every\n   read and write uses.\n2. **Value × reader.** Every value a change writes, against every reader of it (found by searching the field) and every input source the\n   value can come from. A rule over a kind of data lists every writer of that kind. A change to how often something fires is counted\n   against every reader of its output.\n3. **New path × old checks.** For a new input, derived value, mode or changed data shape: every check the old path passes, and whether\n   the new one meets it. A changed shape re-derives every check written for the old one.\n4. **Prior decisions.** The decisions searched for the mechanism by name; any decision that rejected or bounded it is quoted in the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json\nd='\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/'\\\\''\np=json.load(open(d+'\\\\''packet-v1.json'\\\\''))['\\\\''items'\\\\'']\nprint(type(p),p[0].keys(),p[0])\ns=json.load(open('\\\\''poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json'\\\\'')); print('\\\\''seed keys'\\\\'',list(s))\nvs=next(x for x in s.values() if isinstance(x,list) and x and isinstance(x[0],dict))\nprint(vs[0].keys())\nfor idx in (0,1,18,21):\n x=vs[idx]; print('\\\\''seed'\\\\'',idx+1,x.get('\\\\''question'\\\\''),[(r.get('\\\\''lo'\\\\''),r.get('\\\\''hi'\\\\''),r.get('\\\\''condition'\\\\'')) for r in x.get('\\\\''rungs'\\\\'',[])])\nprint('\\\\''packet'\\\\'')\nfor e in p:\n if e.get('\\\\''id'\\\\'') in ('\\\\''i037'\\\\'','\\\\''i090'\\\\'','\\\\''i095'\\\\'','\\\\''i096'\\\\'','\\\\''i129'\\\\'','\\\\''i173'\\\\'','\\\\''i174'\\\\'','\\\\''i218'\\\\'','\\\\''i256'\\\\'','\\\\''i280'\\\\'','\\\\''i281'\\\\'','\\\\''i288'\\\\'') or e.get('\\\\''item_id'\\\\'') in ('\\\\''i037'\\\\'','\\\\''i090'\\\\'','\\\\''i095'\\\\'','\\\\''i096'\\\\'','\\\\''i129'\\\\'','\\\\''i173'\\\\'','\\\\''i174'\\\\'','\\\\''i218'\\\\'','\\\\''i256'\\\\'','\\\\''i280'\\\\'','\\\\''i281'\\\\'','\\\\''i288'\\\\''):\n  print(e)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
